# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Overload turns Mizzium Mortars from one targeted hit into damage to every opposing creature.
# Forcing: Either blocker can stop one attacker if the normal mode removes only the other. Overload clears both, allowing exact-five combat damage.
# AI behavior: The opponent has no responses. Both attackers are ready and both defenders can block.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = Mortars is overloaded, both blockers die, and both attackers deal five.
#   LOSE = normal Mortars removes only one blocker, leaving less than five unblocked power.
#   TIMEOUT = alternate-cost selection or combat did not complete.
# Card roles:
#   Mizzium Mortars — changes target scope with its alternate cost.
#   Friendly Bears and Courser — exact-five attackers.
#   Opposing Bears and Courser — jointly force the overload decision.
# Protocol path: Cast with overload cost, deal four to each opposing creature, then attack.
[metadata]
